WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
At Plant Oxford, new
Minis come off the line,

2
00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.150
bound for over 80 countries.

3
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.570
Its workforce includes 64 nationalities.

4
00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.950
Its owner, BMW Group, is German.

5
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.790
British place.

6
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:13.890
Foreign owner.

7
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.330
Global market.

8
00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:18.470
So what does Made in
Britain mean any more?

9
00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.090
British-owned?

10
00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:20.290
British workers?

11
00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:21.570
Nothing at all?

12
00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:24.590
In this mission, you'll
map who owns the firms,

13
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:28.370
factories and power stations
behind familiar British names.

14
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:33.410
Then you'll ask how global brands and foreign
buyers of land shape national identity,

15
00:00:33.460 --> 00:00:36.190
and how the state responds.

16
00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:41.170
Your mission: decide what Made in
Britain means when the owner is overseas.
